CeCw0waR3De7wvyhZGxx1_an1cHX4xiCewuSahyWDZ3su6bDTJzuVqjW1t137voXDEX126DW6Tqapd8ylGerYQbA9Vocnu3sx3hmSS4pp6HEEg==)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFi_ntAYGK5w1I9jpGr9nFF4ICUT7RuW6O8CyfPmagfAEVUPSRswkIJ-BWUUFVb_YVAPloas3EjhpNRC1DHCThp2-kSrV7gplvswPRNjbjRuwT5fVt-PZmwUVAXDCI4m9dnQKgz6FYO-jbNwDlEebYhVf0Tt2DXa05JskJtuH0xCsSSX4vQpYBUdaFJ0bLruy3q5nQ=)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":858,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:45:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T04:45:29+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:38+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T04:45:29+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:38+08:00\nThe search for \"firestore rest api value types mapValue arrayValue integerValue stringValue booleanValue\" returned the following summary:\nIn the **Cloud Firestore REST API**, every document field value is wrapped in a type-safe object called a **`Value`**[1]. Because the REST API uses explicit typing instead of standard JSON type inference, you must specify the exact data type wrapper for every field (e.g., `stringValue`, `integerValue`, `booleanValue`, `mapValue`, `arrayValue`)[2][3].\n\nBelow is an overview and JSON payload example demonstrating how to use these specific value types in Firestore REST API requests (`POST` or `PATCH`)[4][3].\n\n---\n\n### 1. `stringValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a UTF-8 text string[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** `\"stringValue\": \"your_string_here\"`[3]\n\n### 2. `integerValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a 64-bit integer (`int64`)[1]. \n* **Important:** In the REST API, integer values must be passed as **strings** (e.g., `\"123\"`) to prevent precision loss in languages/environments that handle JSON numbers as standard floating-point types[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** `\"integerValue\": \"42\"` (or sometimes accepted as a raw number depending on the client library, but strictly specified as a string `string (int64 format)` in the official protocol reference)[1].\n\n### 3. `booleanValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a boolean (`true` or `false`)[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** `\"booleanValue\": true`\n\n### 4. `mapValue`\n* **Description:** Represents a nested object or map containing its own set of fields[5]. It wraps a nested `fields` object[5][4].\n* **JSON Syntax:** \n  ```json\n  \"mapValue\": {\n    \"fields\": {\n      \"nestedFieldKey\": { \"stringValue\": \"nested value\" }\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n\n### 5. `arrayValue`\n* **Description:** Represents an ordered list/array of Firestore `Value` items[1]. It wraps an array called `values`[1].\n* **JSON Syntax:** \n  ```json\n  \"arrayVal\n<truncated 163 bytes>\n all of these types together into a standard Firestore REST API document body (e.g., when creating or updating a document)[3]:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"username\": {\n      \"stringValue\": \"johndoe\"\n    },\n    \"age\": {\n      \"integerValue\": \"30\"\n    },\n    \"isActive\": {\n      \"booleanValue\": true\n    },\n    \"tags\": {\n      \"arrayValue\": {\n        \"values\": [\n          { \"stringValue\": \"admin\" },\n          { \"stringValue\": \"developer\" }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"address\": {\n      \"mapValue\": {\n        \"fields\": {\n          \"city\": { \"stringValue\": \"New York\" },\n          \"zipCode\": { \"integerValue\": \"10001\" }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEi6k3_qmcqE1FW5iTFih1Irf9BtgkVsUQzwvOTqwwmDyrsyOmS8blw0eErId-gtTWXOpDwDK5pjU2-9j6b-uZYMQkqOOP4eUizI4hWOzLUcCwaZTVjzfufaE5_Paf-TiNspVBaN2xxraTWkWJLz1O_GHUb3RZWz1D6vSNc4uLiigOGELRC3Q==)\n[2] [gitbook.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHuSuv6OQmixFLSgZM2Nm9filGGWZw-aMADpBVe42oBmVnAeeDN6TNNd8qfCOUCbQRRnn3iOjFMQYAQDJS-BJnurSSYDznL1bZPiHyZA8LxKPALsL5WDBiQnos041d4utxb28DB199CxHtc6hY=)\n[3] [nullisnotanobject.co.uk](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF05LdfqZQ7Rvo5zH7_tiULb3D1GxAaWXkS77QXFHhJyCOkHKJLHRSbDwL--Dt7fR1zkJLQA6moTTjndNU2hvCA5xdq6wCD2vN6mAYpBNCCPPMdJ2DPY9Bn8kdU01N2ofT_mvo2vGvKuZ421Ml4A55eyfZuXXomyQ==)\n[4] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHy7H35yfroooSq69Hz6ZsyOocAT9M9QymIdqRTnATn4bZQBTeeTzGDGganLv4YVOrh8LeOs1dGbvZJN_3e8CkQsXuOEW6i0SSBB5IZJ5ioZz7wTDGGz9Xxf-7yw5C9Twgft700FrXobIo53iCHofjXnBp0Xq5z1OF2ViqvlUIrUkusUQ==)\n[5] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEGMv6idIjf6AldX0EybeqmNew3JTBto5qm3srxMJ2ixokQ6c84dVHljOjfilAkuQhYMUg27QrHCep_UYAJ_LP8XoAHq4XWt6dKDj6TMslirnpnK5eHxi49Ac1U3frMNnQj92ba3FR4DnAGmAorteiZx2-ZsqdG_S3E)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":859,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:45:38Z","input_tokens":3855,"cache_read_tokens":282127,"output_tokens":408,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: direct REST API calls to Firestore should function as expected, even without an authorization token, given the user's open rules. Testing this hypothesis involves verifying that list, create (POST), update (PATCH), and delete operations succeed without authentication and with a null Origin header. This will confirm the system's expected behavior.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"node -e \\\"\\n(async () => {\\n  const base = 'https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/sir-jasper-quiz/databases/(default)/documents';\\n  const g1 = await fetch(base + '/quizzes/active', { headers: { Origin: 'null' } });\\n  console.log('GET active:', g1.status, 'ACAO:', JSON.stringify(g1.headers.get('access-control-allow-origin')));\\n  const g2 = await fetch(base + '/quizzes/active/submissions?orderBy=submittedAt%20desc&pageSize=100', { headers: { Origin: 'null' } });\\n  console.log('LIST submissions orderBy:', g2.status, 'ACAO:', JSON.stringify(g2.headers.get('access-control-allow-origin')));\\n  const c1 = await fetch(base + ':commit', {\\n    method: 'OPTIONS',\\n    headers: { Origin: 'null', 'Access-Control-Request-Method': 'POST', 'Access-Control-Request-Headers': 'content-type' }\\n  });\\n  console.log('OPTIONS commit:', c1.status, 'ACAO:', JSON.stringify(c1.headers.get('access-control-allow-origin')));\\n})();\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Test Firestore REST list orderBy and CORS\""}}]}
