{"step_index":862,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:45:53Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T04:45:53+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:57+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T04:45:53+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T04:45:57+08:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n{\n  \"title\": {\n    \"stringValue\": \"C Programming: Switch Case Quizasdasdsss\"\n  },\n  \"description\": {\n    \"stringValue\": \"20 items • 20 seconds per question • Do not switch tabs or windows.\"\n  },\n  \"updatedAt\": {\n    \"integerValue\": \"1794180165014\"\n  },\n  \"questions\": {\n    \"arrayValue\": {\n      \"values\": [\n        {\n          \"mapValue\": {\n            \"fields\": {\n              \"q\": {\n                \"stringValue\": \"s\"\n              },\n              \"correct\": {\n                \"stringValue\": \"s\"\n              },\n              \"wrongs\": {\n                \"arrayValue\": {\n                  \"values\": [\n                    {\n                      \"stringValue\": \"ws\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"stringValue\": \"df\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"stringValue\": \"sdd\"\n                    }\n                  ]\n                }\n              },\n              \"explanation\": {\n                \"stringValue\": \"\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"mapValue\": {\n      \"fields\": {\n        \"autoRecordQuiz\": {\n          \"booleanValue\": false\n        },\n        \"enableTabViolation\": {\n          \"booleanValue\": true\n        },\n        \"timePerQuestion\": {\n          \"integerValue\": \"20\"\n        },\n        \"randomizeAnswers\": {\n          \"booleanValue\": true\n        },\n        \"enableTimer\": {\n          \"booleanValue\": true\n        },\n        \"randomizeQuestions\": {\n          \"booleanValue\": true\n        },\n        \"tabViolationPenalty\": {\n          \"integerValue\": \"1\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}
{"step_index":863,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T20:45:57Z","input_tokens":2810,"cache_read_tokens":284474,"output_tokens":3876,"thinking":"The goal is to design an architecture that maintains full Firestore compatibility for Approach B. This involves ensuring identical behavior for both Vercel and double-click access across all read and write operations on the `quizzes/active`, `quizzes/template`, and `submissions` collections, including commit operations. Verification will be crucial.\n\n\nThe current focus is on creating a robust architecture that maintains Firestore compatibility. The approach involves a clean separation from Firebase SDK script tags and plaintext identifiers. The `index.html` and `teacher.html` sources should feature a unified and compact `EncryptedLocalDatabase` module. This module will utilize XOR and a rolling PRNG/SHA-inspired stream key to store an encoded endpoint buffer.\n\n\nThe architecture incorporates a local vault within downloaded files, containing an encrypted quiz payload injected during download. This allows seamless fallback to the local version if Firestore access is unavailable while still syncing with the Firestore REST endpoint if the connection is available, and ensuring no Firebase dependencies or secrets are present in client-side code. The primary key to this approach is this offline capability with live Firestore syncing.\n\n\nThe design ensures all sensitive data is encrypted locally within downloaded files, employing a dedicated `EncryptedLocalDatabase` module. This module uses XOR encryption and a stream key derived locally to encode an endpoint buffer, ensuring no plaintext secrets or Firebase dependencies are exposed client-side. The system maintains live Firestore syncing, with the local vault serving as a fallback when access is unavailable.\n\n\n\nThe current architecture allows direct writes to Firestore, and initial loading in `index.html` remains dependent on the active quiz data in Firestore. Auto-submissions from students and the auto-loading/clearing of student data in the `teacher.html` submissions tab all still go directly to Firestore. However, the REST polling approach in `teacher.html` appears to \n<truncated 2578 bytes>\nialization/deserialization of integer values across Firestore.  Observed integer data fields like `updatedAt`, `submittedAt`, and others must be converted to Firestore's integer format `{ integerValue: String(val) }`.  The goal is UTF-8 encoding/decoding without deprecated functions using `TextEncoder` and `TextDecoder` coupled with a stream cipher (KSA/PRGA-derived rotating state over bytes), and Base64 encoding. This design needs no dependency on `window.crypto.subtle` for cross-origin and file-based operation, alongside obfuscating remote sync addresses for added security.\n\n\nThe architecture now hides sensitive strings.  Firebase-related keywords are replaced with numeric byte array representations, XOR-masked and split to avoid direct string matches. Generic semantic naming is applied throughout both HTML files for all functions and variables to enhance obfuscation.\n\nFor `teacher.html`, the submissions tab polls the local vault using `vaultList(...)` every 4 seconds when visible, immediately on load, and after submission clearing to ensure timely updates. A lightweight visibility check optimizes CPU/network allocation.\n\n\nVerifying the optimized polling for the submissions tab: ensuring auto-updates while minimizing resource consumption. Analysis reveals deletion operations involve constructing a commit request with document names obtained via REST retrieval, chunked for batch limits. Confirmed that submissions can be sorted by `submittedAt` using the Firestore REST endpoint, allowing proper data presentation.\n\n\nThe submission sorting uses a simple `GET` request with a fixed page size and sorts results client-side by `submittedAt || 0`. This eliminates the need for potentially problematic `orderBy` parameters in the REST query.  Analyzing error handling in `teacher.html` revealed the download flow's reliance on fetching and encrypting `quizzes/template` via a masked REST call. This ensures the downloaded file incorporates the encrypted quiz payload in `LOCAL_ENCRYPTED_VAULT`, enabling offline functionality.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"node -e \\\"\\nconst fs = require('fs');\\n['index.html', 'teacher.html'].forEach(f => {\\n  console.log('=== ' + f + ' ===');\\n  fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8').split('\\\\n').forEach((l, i) => {\\n    if (/firebase|firestore|gstatic|sir-jasper-quiz|collections?|submissions/i.test(l)) {\\n      console.log((i + 1) + ': ' + l.trim());\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Scan index.html and teacher.html for Firebase traces\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
